<title>USA: W.R. Grace &amp; Co Q4 loss narrows.</title>
<headline>W.R. Grace &amp; Co Q4 loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr loss	    $1.44     loss	 $2.82</p>
<p> Net shr loss	     $0.70     loss	 $4.87</p>
<p> Net loss		  56,800     loss     473,800</p>
<p> Revs		     863,000		  934,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  81,400		   97,300</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)  </p>
<p>			  Year</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	  $2.32     loss	 $1.87</p>
<p> Net shr profit	  $31.06     loss	 $3.40</p>
<p> Net profit	   2,857,700     loss     325,900</p>
<p> Revs		   3,493,000		3,593,800</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  92,000		   95,800</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Revs figures include sales and other income. Q4 sales were $850.8 million vs $905.2 million. Full year sales were $3.45 billion vs $3.55 billion.  </p>
<p>Net share figures include discontinued operations gain of $0.74 a share vs loss $2.05 in Q4, and gain of $28.74 a share vs loss $1.53 for the full year.</p>
<p>1996 discontinued operations gains result from health care segment operating results and gains on disposition of NMC, Amicon and Agracetus, as well as operating losses for TEC Systems.</p>
<p>1995 results restated to reflect classification of health care segment and TEC Systems as discontinued operations.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
</text>
